<title>USA: Neiman Marcus Q3 shr $0.41 vs $0.30.</title>
<headline>Neiman Marcus Q3 shr $0.41 vs $0.30.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.41		    $0.30</p>
<p> Net			 20,718		   18,797</p>
<p> Revs		     506,532		  474,059</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  50,026		   38,224</p>
<p>     9   MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.05		    $1.17</p>
<p> Net			 77,235		   66,671</p>
<p> Revs		   1,712,582		1,589,381</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  46,439		   38,184</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full name is Neiman Marcus Group Inc.</p>
<p>For the 39 weeks ended May 3, 1997, operating earnings rose 12.8 percent to $151.3 million from $134.1 million a year earlier, while net earnings before a non-recurring charge increased 15.8 percent to $77.2 million from $66.7 million.</p>
<p>For the 39 weeks, after preferred dividends and before a non-recurring charge related to early redemption of preferred stock, earnings per share were $1.53 vs $1.17.</p>
<p>The non-recurring after-tax charge totaled $22.4 million, or $0.48 per share, for the 39 weeks ended May 3, 1997.</p>
